Fillets: a rounding cut at its end by a periodic face whose seam starts at
the corner's vertex (mitcad#236).

Where the face at the end of a rounding (OnDiff or AllSame corner) is
periodic and its seam starts at the corner's vertex (a cylinder whose seam
runs from that vertex), the two arcs that hold the rounding's contacts have
their curves on the face on the two sides of the seam, a period apart. The
intersection of the blend with the face was then sought between two points
almost a period apart: it came out running nearly round the whole face, and
crossing the other roundings' ends on the face ("OneCorner : fillets have
too big radiuses").

- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner: the second point on the face at the
  end is taken in the period within half a period of the first one, in u
  and in v. The intersection then runs the short way across the seam, and
  is cut at the seam as before (the "couture" case).

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
index 26d1498..6992da4 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_C1.cxx
@@ -1740,6 +1740,24 @@ void ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner(const int Index, const bool thePrepareOnSa
     {
       ChFi3d_Recale(Bs, pfac1, pfac2, (IFadArc == 1));
     }
+    else
+    {
+      // The two points in one period of a periodic face at the end: where
+      // the face's seam starts at the corner's vertex, the arcs' curves on
+      // the face lie on the seam's two sides, a period apart, and the
+      // intersection, which crosses the seam (cut there below), was sought
+      // round the whole face.
+      if (Bs.IsUPeriodic())
+      {
+        const double T = Bs.UPeriod();
+        pfac2.SetX(ElCLib::InPeriod(pfac2.X(), pfac1.X() - 0.5 * T, pfac1.X() + 0.5 * T));
+      }
+      if (Bs.IsVPeriodic())
+      {
+        const double T = Bs.VPeriod();
+        pfac2.SetY(ElCLib::InPeriod(pfac2.Y(), pfac1.Y() - 0.5 * T, pfac1.Y() + 0.5 * T));
+      }
+    }
 
     Pardeb(1) = pfil1.X();
     Pardeb(2) = pfil1.Y();
